From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JSBedded <noreply@jsbedded.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add CONFIG_NO_ATOMICS and CONFIG_NO_MALLOC_USABLE_SIZE

Local-only (not sent upstream yet): bare-metal and RTOS targets build
QuickJS without OS threads or a libc malloc_usable_size().

- CONFIG_ATOMICS is defined unconditionally outside Emscripten and pulls
  in <pthread.h>, pthread mutexes/condition variables and clock_gettime().
  arm-none-eabi newlib (pico-sdk) has no pthreads, so the build fails.
  CONFIG_NO_ATOMICS leaves Atomics out, as the Emscripten build already does.
- js_def_malloc_usable_size() calls malloc_usable_size() without a
  declaration on non-glibc libcs (<malloc.h> is only included on
  Linux/glibc), which is an error with GCC >= 14 (ESP-IDF v6).
  CONFIG_NO_MALLOC_USABLE_SIZE returns 0 there, as upstream's comment
  suggests. JSBedded installs its own allocator, so the default one is
  unused anyway.
---
 quickjs.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index fa5a7a9..d3cc84a 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -67,8 +67,9 @@
 #endif
 
 /* define to include Atomics.* operations which depend on the OS
-   threads */
-#if !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+   threads. Define CONFIG_NO_ATOMICS to leave them out on targets
+   without threads (no pthreads needed then). */
+#if !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) && !defined(CONFIG_NO_ATOMICS)
 #define CONFIG_ATOMICS
 #endif
 
@@ -2140,7 +2141,7 @@ static size_t js_def_malloc_usable_size(const void *ptr)
     return malloc_size(ptr);
 #elif defined(_WIN32)
     return _msize((void *)ptr);
-#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(CONFIG_NO_MALLOC_USABLE_SIZE)
     return 0;
 #elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__GLIBC__)
     return malloc_usable_size((void *)ptr);
